      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:1:21:8",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) أَيُّمَا مُؤْمِنٍ أَوْصَلَ إِلَى أَخِيهِ الْمُؤْمِنِ مَعْرُوفاً فَقَدْ أَوْصَلَ ذَلِكَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Al Hassan Bin Mahboub, from Jameel Bin Darraj, from Hadeed Bin Hakeym or Murazam who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Whichever Believer brings an act of kindness to his brother, so he has brought it to Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from al-Hassan ibn Mahbub from Jamil ibn Darraj from Hadid ibn Hakim or Murazim who has said the following: ‘Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If a believing person maintains good relations with his brother in belief, he is considered as maintaining such relations with the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
